<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had sown 82.9 percent of their 1997/98 wheat crop by Aug 8, the Agriculture Secretariat said in its weekly report Thursday.</p>
<p>This compared with 93.0 percent completion of a larger sown area by the same date last season. A lack of rain for three weeks has allowed farmers in many water-logged areas to complete their fieldwork. Wheat sown in Buenos Aires province is developing well, despite heavy frosts in the week to August 8. Fertilizer use in the province has not fallen much from last year. Wheat in parts of Cordoba is in bad shape and stressed due by lack of water. South Santa Fe wheat is in good shape.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets).</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..............</p>
<p> Wheat     6,250  82.9  (93.0)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)</p>
<p> Maize     3,952  100.0(100.0) 3,234.6   99.6  (99.3)</p>
<p> Soybeans  6,648  100.0(100.0)     n/a  100.0 (100.0)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,048  100.0(100.0)     n/a  100.0 (100.0)</p>
<p> Sorghum     805  100.0(100.0)     n/a  100.0 (100.0)</p>
<p> Cotton	956  100.0  (n/a)   882.6   99.4  (98.0)</p>
